       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nThe intended dose may have been one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max IR dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's above the maximum recommended dose and was intentional."
